        "goal": "Load the survey collection, photos and video together.",
        "metadata": {
          "keywords": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "survey-gallery",
        "type": "curio.builtin/vis-simple",
        "x": 645,
        "y": 0,
        "content": "",
        "out": "DEFAULT",
        "in": "DEFAULT",
        "goal": "Show every file as a card; the video plays in its card.",
        "metadata": {
          "keywords": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "survey-map",
        "type": "curio.builtin/vis-vega",
        "x": 645,
        "y": 860,
        "content": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v6.json\",\n  \"description\": \"Where each photo was taken.\",\n  \"mark\": {\n    \"type\": \"circle\",\n    \"size\": 80\n  },\n  \"encoding\": {\n    \"longitude\": {\n      \"field\": \"gps_lon\",\n      \"type\": \"quantitative\"\n    },\n    \"latitude\": {\n      \"field\": \"gps_lat\",\n      \"type\": \"quantitative\"\n    },\n    \"color\": {\n      \"field\": \"kind\",\n      \"type\": \"nominal\",\n      \"title\": \"File\"\n    },\n    \"tooltip\": [\n      {\n        \"field\": \"name\",\n        \"type\": \"nominal\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"field\": \"taken_at\",\n        \"type\": \"temporal\",\n        \"timeUnit\": \"utcyearmonthdatehoursminutes\",\n        \"title\": \"taken\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n",
        "out": "DEFAULT",
        "in": "DEFAULT",
        "goal": "Map where each file was taken.",
        "metadata": {
          "keywords": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "survey-frames",
        "type": "curio.media/video-frames",
        "x": 645,
        "y": 430,
        "content": "\"\"\"Sample Video Frames.\n\nInput: a collection's rows, as Data Loading's `curio_load_collection(...)` returns\nthem. Every video row becomes one row per sampled frame, and each frame is a\nJPEG written beside the collection's other derived files. A frame row has the\ncolumns of an image row (`path`, `thumbnail`, `image_url`, `width`, `height`),\nso Simple View shows the frames and any node that reads images reads them. It\nalso keeps the video's own columns: its fields, its position, and its time,\nmoved forward by the frame's offset. `t_s` is the frame's time in the video,\nand `frame` its number there.\n\nThe Widgets tab sets the gap between two sampled frames, in seconds, and the\nmost frames kept from one video.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom media_collections import sample_video_frames\n\nreturn sample_video_frames(\n    input_0, curio_derived_file,\n    every_seconds=float([!! every_seconds !!]),\n    max_frames_per_video=int([!! max_frames_per_video !!]),\n)\n",
        "out": "DEFAULT",
        "in": "DEFAULT",
        "goal": "Sample a frame every quarter second from the video.",
        "metadata": {
          "keywords": [],
          "widgets": [
            {
              "name": "every_seconds",
              "type": "number",
              "label": "Gap between frames",
              "default": 2.0,
              "options": {
                "units": "s"
              },
              "value": 0.25
            },
            {
              "name": "max_frames_per_video",
              "type": "number",
              "label": "Maximum frames per video",
              "default": 300,
              "options": {
                "step": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "survey-frames-view",
        "type": "curio.builtin/vis-simple",
        "x": 1290,
        "y": 430,
        "content": "",
        "out": "DEFAULT",
        "in": "DEFAULT",
        "goal": "Show the sampled frames.",
        "metadata": {
          "keywords": []
        }
      }
    ],
